MQTT-Based Real-Time Student Notification and Academic Announcement System

============================================================
1) WHAT IS INCLUDED IN THIS ROOT FOLDER
============================================================

1. backend/            -> Node.js + Express API + MQTT publisher + scheduler + FCM hook
2. web-dashboard/      -> React web app for Admin and Teacher
3. mobile-app/         -> Expo React Native app for Student
4. database.sql        -> MySQL schema + sample seed users/data
5. SETUP_AND_RUN_GUIDE.doc -> This run guide


============================================================
2) REQUIRED INSTALLATIONS (PREREQUISITES)
============================================================

Install these before running:

1. Node.js LTS (includes npm)
2. XAMPP (for MySQL)
3. Eclipse Mosquitto MQTT Broker
4. Expo Go app on Android/iOS phone (for mobile testing)
5. (Optional for FCM) Firebase Project + Service Account JSON


============================================================
3) IMPORTANT PORTS
============================================================

Backend API (Node/Express):         http://localhost:5000
Web Dashboard (Vite React):         http://localhost:5173
Mobile App (Expo Dev Server):       http://localhost:8081 (typical Metro port)
MySQL (XAMPP):                      3306
Mosquitto MQTT TCP:                 1883
Mosquitto MQTT over WebSocket:      9001 (for React Native MQTT ws://)


============================================================
4) DATABASE SETUP (XAMPP MYSQL)
============================================================

1. Start Apache and MySQL in XAMPP Control Panel.
2. Open phpMyAdmin.
3. Import the file: database.sql
4. This creates:
   - student_notification_system DB
   - users, subjects, sections, notifications, student_subjects,
     notification_reads, fcm_tokens tables
   - sample accounts

Sample Accounts:
Admin:   admin@school.com    / admin123
Teacher: teacher1@school.com / teacher123
Student: student1@school.com / student123


============================================================
5) MOSQUITTO SETUP
============================================================

Use Mosquitto with both TCP and WebSocket listeners.

Example mosquitto.conf entries:

listener 1883
protocol mqtt

listener 9001
protocol websockets

Then restart Mosquitto.


============================================================
6) BACKEND SETUP & RUN
============================================================

1. Go to backend folder.
2. Copy .env.example to .env
3. Update DB and MQTT values if needed.
4. Run:

   npm install -----
   npm run dev

Health check:
GET http://localhost:5000/api/health

Optional FCM setup:
- Put Firebase service account JSON as:
  backend/firebase-service-account.json


============================================================
7) WEB DASHBOARD SETUP & RUN
============================================================

1. Go to web-dashboard folder
2. Run:

   npm install
   npm run dev

3. Open browser:
   http://localhost:5173

Use Admin account to create teacher/section/subject.
Use Teacher account to send instant or scheduled notifications.


============================================================
8) MOBILE APP SETUP & RUN (EXPO GO)
============================================================

1. Go to mobile-app/src/config.js
2. Update values to your PC LAN IP:

   API_URL = 'http://<YOUR_PC_IP>:5000/api'
   MQTT_BROKER_WS_URL = 'ws://<YOUR_PC_IP>:9001'

3. Go to mobile-app folder and run:

   npm install
   npm start

4. Scan QR code with Expo Go app.
5. Login as student account.


============================================================
9) HOW THE SYSTEM FLOWS
============================================================

Teacher sends notification -> Backend saves to DB ->
Backend publishes MQTT topic school/{section}/{subject} ->
Online students receive real-time ->
Backend also sends push notification through FCM hook (if configured).


============================================================
10) NOTES
============================================================

1. Passwords in this project are plain text by request.
2. For production, use password hashing + HTTPS + stricter token security.
3. If mobile cannot connect, check firewall and ensure phone + PC are same Wi-Fi.
